  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="80">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has no gender capacity building plans, the partner is the    University of Hargeisa and they   have  been implementing access to justice programing with different  aid donors and agencies .
UOH  aspires to become a leading national center ofeducational excellence that meets the nation&#x2019;s immediate and long-term goals for education and  human development.
Oxfam has established the Ignite Career Hub at the University of Hargeisa, funded by the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs as part of the LEAD Programme, to address the challenge of youth unemployment in Somaliland. The center provides young people with 21st century skills and links them with job opportunities to help them enter the job market. The University of Hargeisa was selected as thehost of the career center, based on its status as a state university, ownership of premises, and capacity to run and sustain the center&apos;s operations</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">University of Hargeisa</narrative>
  </participating-org>
